{"name":"Splinter","hex":"#a3713f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Splinter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Splinter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Splinter","blocks":[{"text":"A splinter is a fragment of a larger object, or a foreign body that becomes embedded in a body. To be considered a splinter, the foreign body must penetrate and remain lodged within the tissue. Splinters may cause initial pain due to the damage of flesh and muscle, and can cause an infection through contamination by bacteria on the foreign object."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Splinter.jpg/330px-Splinter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splinter","wikidata":"Q2510520"},{"title":"Splinter (Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles)","blocks":[{"text":"Splinter, often referred to as Master Splinter or Sensei by his students/sons, is a fictional character from Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles comics and all related media. A mutant rat, he is the grave and stoic sage of the Turtles, their ninjutsu and martial arts instructor, and their adoptive father."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/Splinter_%28character%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splinter_(Teenage_Mutant_Ninja_Turtles)","wikidata":"Q2082114"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Sea_Urchins_enjoying_sunbathing.jpg/500px-Sea_Urchins_enjoying_sunbathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Sea_Urchins_enjoying_sunbathing.jpg/1280px-Sea_Urchins_enjoying_sunbathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t